From: LuneOS port <webos-ports@webos-ports.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mrdump: fix %llx format for 32-bit phys_addr_t

On arm32 without LPAE phys_addr_t is 32-bit, and gcc under
-Werror=format rejects printing it with %llx. Cast explicitly.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, no upstream]
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/aee/mrdump/mrdump_panic.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/aee/mrdump/mrdump_panic.c
index 1769cd6a9984..ac2218cd9aae 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/aee/mrdump/mrdump_panic.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/aee/mrdump/mrdump_panic.c
@@ -250,8 +250,9 @@ static __init int mrdump_parse_chosen(void)
 			mrdump_sram_cb.start_addr = reg[0];
 			mrdump_sram_cb.size = reg[1];
 			pr_notice("%s: mrdump_cbaddr=%llx, mrdump_cbsize=%llx\n",
-				  __func__, mrdump_sram_cb.start_addr,
-				  mrdump_sram_cb.size);
+				  __func__,
+				  (unsigned long long)mrdump_sram_cb.start_addr,
+				  (unsigned long long)mrdump_sram_cb.size);
 		}
 
 		if (of_property_read_string(node, "mrdump,lk", &lkver) == 0) {
